(in-ns 'go.arbace.pyctypes) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The C API's natives the class :capi-port still named after py-capi-1122 (the burst of 2026-11-25, py-capi-1125;"] [4 1 "// doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: py-capi-1125\"), each written after CPython 3.14.10's function of the same"] [5 1 "// name: PyErr_Display, PyErr_DisplayException, PyErr_Print and PyErr_PrintEx (Python/pythonrun.c), PyCode_Addr2Line"] [6 1 "// (Objects/codeobject.c) and Py_UniversalNewlineFgets (Objects/fileobject.c). The PSF's license (LICENSE.md)."] [17 1 "// cThreads are the C threads PyThread_start_new_thread made, by their Python thread's ident (each a Python thread"] [18 1 "// of _thread's, so the GIL serializes them with the others)."] [21 1 "// cLocks are PyThread_allocate_lock's locks (Python/thread_pthread.h): each a _thread.lock of pyi's (blocking with"] [22 1 "// the GIL released, as PyThread_acquire_lock runs under Py_BEGIN_ALLOW_THREADS in CPython), by the address of the"] [23 1 "// 8 bytes of the world that is the PyThread_type_lock C holds."] [26 1 "// cThreadStack is a C thread's stack (as musl's default for pthread_create: 128 KiB is musl's, the world's C code is"] [27 1 "// CPython's test modules', so 1 MiB)."] [30 1 "// The world's lock (py-capi-1125): while a C thread lives, one Python thread at a time is inside the C world, from its"] [31 1 "// entry (World.Call, a C thread's start) to its return, nested Python code included; the owner gives it up only while it"] [32 1 "// waits in PyThread_acquire_lock (CPython's callers hold no GIL there: Py_BEGIN_ALLOW_THREADS). Without it a thread's C"] [33 1 "// would run while another's is suspended in Python code a native called, and the error indicator and the mirrors'"] [34 1 "// bookkeeping (errIndicator, touched), which are the world's and not a thread's, would be mixed. A waiter blocks on a"] [35 1 "// _thread.lock of its own, so the GIL is released while it waits; the bookkeeping is the GIL holder's. Off while no C"] [36 1 "// thread lives: the depth of each Python thread inside C (cEntryDepth) is kept so that the starter, inside C, owns it at"] [37 1 "// once."] [54 1 "// wlTake makes the running thread (id) the owner with n levels, waiting its turn when another owns it."] [75 54 "// released by the handoff (wlGive)"] [79 1 "// wlGive gives up all of the owner's levels: the first waiter owns it next (its lock released), else no one."] [91 1 "// enterC and exitC bracket an entry into the C world (World.Call; a C thread's start)."] [95 19 "// the globals are this thread's entry state (cThreadSwitch)"] [116 1 "// wlOn turns the lock on at a C thread's start: the starter (inside C) owns it with its depth."] [128 1 "// wlOff turns it off once no C thread lives and no one waits."] [135 1 "// blockingWait runs f (a wait that releases the GIL) with the world's lock given up, the error indicator and the mirrors'"] [136 1 "// bookkeeping of the running native kept across it, then takes the lock back with the levels it had."] [152 1 "// startCThread is PyThread_start_new_thread(func, arg): a Python thread of _thread's whose body runs the C function"] [153 1 "// func(arg) on a C thread of its own (a stack mapped in the world, the main thread's thread-local objects), the"] [154 1 "// mirrors synchronized around it as around a call into C; a fault in it ends the process (World.guard). Its ident,"] [155 1 "// or -1 when the thread cannot start."] [196 1 "// lockOf is the _thread.lock of a PyThread_type_lock (a fault for one PyThread_allocate_lock did not give, as a freed"] [197 1 "// pthread lock's use is undefined)."] [206 1 "// thread is the C thread of the running Python thread: the one PyThread_start_new_thread made for it (capi_rest.go,"] [207 1 "// py-capi-1125), the world's main thread (the library's) for the interpreter's main thread, else one of its own, made"] [208 1 "// on the thread's first entry (pyThreads). The GIL's holder is the only goroutine that runs C, so each Python thread's C"] [209 1 "// frames stay on a stack of its own."] [233 1 "// pyThreads are the C threads of the Python threads but the main one (py-regress-1127, train 7's records: every Python"] [234 1 "// thread ran its C on the world's main thread, so that a thread whose C was suspended in Python code a native called (a"] [235 1 "// reducer of the C _pickle's, the GIL handed over) had its frames overwritten by another's C, test_process_pool's spawn"] [236 1 "// workers' \"segmentation fault in the C world\" in batch_dict_exact and save): a stack of cThreadStack mapped in the world"] [237 1 "// at the thread's first entry (CPython's THREAD_STACK_SIZE on musl), the main thread's thread-local objects and task, as"] [238 1 "// a C thread's; unmapped when the Python thread ends (cThreadEnded)."] [241 1 "// cThreadEnded is py's ExtThreadEnd for the world: the ended Python thread's C stack unmapped, its saved entry state"] [242 1 "// dropped."] [250 18 "// its entry state is done with: the next thread to take the GIL finds its own"] [254 1 "// The world's entry state by thread (py-regress-1127): the error indicator, the mirrors a native used (touched), the"] [255 1 "// nesting of World.Call and the lists its natives used (worldDepth, usedLists) and the thread state's context"] [256 1 "// (tsCtx and the context slot C reads) are a Python thread's, as CPython's thread state is: when the GIL changes hands"] [257 1 "// (py's ExtThreadSwitch) the leaving thread's are saved and the taking thread's put back, so that a thread whose C is"] [258 1 "// suspended in Python code a native called finds them as it left them, whatever another thread's C did meanwhile."] [259 1 "// cDepth stays the world's: the borrowed references of every suspended entry stay valid until the last returns."] [266 17 "// the context slot's word at ts when the thread left (C may have cleared it)"] [271 21 "// the thread whose state the globals hold (0: none yet)"] [274 1 "// cThreadSwitch is py's ExtThreadSwitch: the running thread took the GIL from another. The leaving thread's state is"] [275 1 "// kept when it has one (inside C, or an error indicator left set); nothing is done when neither has one (a hand-off"] [276 1 "// between threads outside C). usedLists only counts inside an entry (World.Call makes a new one at the outermost)."] [315 1 "// displayException is _PyErr_Display(file, NULL, value, tb): a traceback given beside an exception that has none"] [316 1 "// put on it (issue #18776), then traceback._print_exception_bltin(value), which writes sys.stderr (colorized when"] [317 1 "// _colorize says so); when that cannot run, sys.__excepthook__'s own printing."] [332 2 "// the fallback: the built-in hook's printing of the same exception"] [345 1 "// writeStderr is PySys_WriteStderr of a text: sys.stderr.write(s), its errors ignored."] [352 1 "// handleSystemExit is _Py_HandleSystemExit and Py_Exit for an exception that is a SystemExit: its code (None 0, an int"] [353 1 "// its value, anything else printed to sys.stderr and 1), the exit functions run (atexit's, Py_FinalizeEx's first step)"] [354 1 "// and the standard streams flushed, then the process exits. false (nothing done) for any other exception."] [393 1 "// printEx is _PyErr_PrintEx: the raised exception (none: nothing) handed to sys.excepthook(type, value, traceback),"] [394 1 "// sys.last_exc, last_type, last_value and last_traceback set first when setSysLastVars, the audit event"] [395 1 "// \"sys.excepthook\" raised before the call; a hook that fails has its error and the original displayed, a missing hook"] [396 1 "// \"sys.excepthook is missing\" and the exception displayed. A SystemExit exits the process (handle_system_exit)."] [459 1 "// lineOfOffset is PyCode_Addr2Line's _PyCode_CheckLineNumber over code.co_lines(): the line of the range holding the"] [460 1 "// byte offset addr (-1 for a range of no line, or an offset no range holds)."] [490 1 "// fgetsByte is the stream's next byte as getc gives it (-1 at the end or on an error), read by the world's fread into"] [491 1 "// one byte of the world's memory."] [504 1 "// ungetByte is musl's ungetc of a byte just read by fread: the read position stepped back over the buffer's byte"] [505 1 "// (rpos at offset 8 of musl's FILE, never below its buffer after a read of it) and the end-of-file flag (F_EOF, 16)"] [506 1 "// cleared. EOF is not pushed back."] [524 2 "// PyErr_Display(unused, value, tb) and PyErr_DisplayException(exc) (Python/pythonrun.c): the exception printed to"] [525 2 "// sys.stderr as the interpreter prints an uncaught one (traceback's _print_exception_bltin)"] [538 2 "// PyErr_Print() is PyErr_PrintEx(1); the error indicator cleared"] [547 2 "// PyCode_Addr2Line(code, addrq) (Objects/codeobject.c): co_firstlineno for a negative offset, else the line of the"] [548 2 "// address range that holds it (code.co_lines(), the location table's view)"] [572 2 "// Py_UniversalNewlineFgets(buf, n, stream, fobj) (Objects/fileobject.c, _Py_UniversalNewlineFgetsWithSize): at most"] [573 2 "// n-1 bytes of the line, \\r and \\r\\n read as \\n, NUL-terminated; NULL when nothing was read; fobj must be NULL"] [574 2 "// (errno ENXIO otherwise)"] [580 21 "// ENXIO"] [609 2 "// the thread module's natives (Python/thread.c, thread_pthread.h)"] [620 3 "// the world's malloc'd 8 bytes, freed by PyThread_free_lock (not a cbuf, which the collector frees)"] [636 2 "// PyThread_acquire_lock(lock, waitflag): 1 (PY_LOCK_ACQUIRED) or 0; PyThread_acquire_lock_timed(lock, microseconds,"] [637 2 "// intr_flag): microseconds < 0 waits as long as it takes, 0 does not wait"] [673 3 "// a lock not held stays released (thread_pthread.h's semaphore lock posts; the error is no one's to see)"] [677 2 "// PySlice_Unpack (queue 262's, capi_limited.go) when an index of the slice is no int or None: its __index__ is Python"] [678 2 "// code that may change any object C sees (gh-72054: test_slice's PopIndex pops from the list whose Py_SIZE the"] [679 2 "// macro PySlice_GetIndicesEx reads after the call), so the mirrors are synchronized around it as around a call"] [680 2 "// into C: C's writes taken first, then Go's state written back to C"] [696 1 "// plainIndex is a slice index whose evaluation runs no Python code: None or an exact int."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[105 22] [109 16] [123 25] [213 23] [220 23] [244 23] [301 24] [322 31] [323 57] [327 63] [328 44] [333 52] [335 57] [340 43] [347 43] [368 23] [369 25] [373 29] [374 26] [381 52] [385 40] [411 55] [425 45] [430 85] [431 23] [438 56] [443 46] [480 34] [527 23] [533 23] [579 23] [585 13] [585 23] [630 37] [653 23] [681 44]]} (go/file "capi_rest.go" :imports [

